":"A","u":"6Gbd1KCtlOyIzo3LHNPGcQ%3D%3D","c":"45"}],"q":null,"nivel":"insuficiente"}},"hash":"c0fbd0d10ca54f76","ia":{"es":"Qué muestran los datos: Entre 2023 y 2025, este organismo adjudicó 34 contratos menores de servicios y suministros de más de 14.000 y hasta 15.000 euros, justo por debajo del límite legal. Si esos importes se repartieran como en la franja inmediatamente inferior, lo esperable serían 9,4 contratos. La razón entre observados y esperados es 3,6, con un intervalo de confianza del 95 % de 2,3 a 5,7. En diciembre se adjudicó el 9 % de los contratos junto al límite, mientras que diciembre supone el 7 % de todos sus contratos de servicios y suministros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 29 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.850 euros, se adjudicó en noviembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: La concentración de contratos al límite no refleja actos ilícitos. Puede deberse a decisiones basadas en precios de mercado o necesidades específicas. No implica que se hayan cometido errores en la contratación.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos al límite se reparten entre varios proveedores. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en áreas similares. Analizar si los contratos se agrupan en un periodo específico, como diciembre.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 34 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 9.4 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 3.6, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.3 to 5.7. December accounts for 9% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 7% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 29 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,850 euros, was awarded in November 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The data shows that some contracts are just under the limit, but it doesn't prove any wrongdoing. Prices might be lower than expected, or budgets might be fixed. There could be other reasons for the amounts being just under the limit.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and amounts of the contracts to see if they follow a pattern. Look at awardee A's contracts to see if they are repeated or if they cover the same needs. Review contract [1] to see what was purchased and how it fits within the budget.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["s139IqJcxu8aF6cS8TCh%2FA%3D%3D","uO4MIXyo8dMZDGvgaZEVxQ%3D%3D","whdMC7tbsvYeIBJRHQiPkQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}